  "body": "Validate the source-built SDK3 in the pinned existing image and continue toward official MD-V3 strict repeats. SDK3 is a single read-only per-container overlay; original SDK/image and every previous request/verdict stay unchanged.\n\nActual results:\n- Run 43824577772 (artifact 14205942495): three SDK3 processes reached core/GLX objects and cleanup without SIGABRT. All six tiny frames were black and children exited 1; this attempt remains failed. Loader traces independently match all 110 previously explained version bindings to libc in each process.\n- Run 43827976143 (artifact 14206869856): corrected ownership keeps Xvfb alive through native child finalization. All five probes exit 0. Both original-wheel/manual and SDK3/manual controls remain black; original-wheel/ShowBase and both SDK3/ShowBase probes pass their exact two fresh 8x8 RGB challenges, softpipe identity and cleanup. Only the two successful SDK3 standard-path probes qualify selected GLX behavior; no universal full C++ ABI claim.\n- The first conditional official model process (PID 11) loaded ORT and began original MetaDrive 0.4.3 initialization, then was killed by the 4 GiB cgroup limit. No trial or strict pair completed. It is retained separately; the original strict 0/4 FAIL result is unchanged.\n\nThe new model-only source authenticates the immutable selected GLX carrier and recomputes its raw pixels/exit/lifecycle/independence. It requires 12 GiB host memory available for bounded 10 GiB model containers, then starts a fresh four-condition/eight-process cohort with unchanged model bytes, original PSSM/Chase, 964x604 source cameras, recurrence/actions and exact comparison. Expansion requires 4/4. No model weights enter Git or result artifacts.\n\nValidation: 20 focused evidence/lifecycle tests pass. Previous exact-source canonical suites passed 1903 and 1907 cases / 7 skips; current exact-source canonical CI is pending. Sole fresh whole-branch review completed; four Important issues fixed RED\u2192GREEN in one pass, no deferred Minors or rereview. Subsequent runtime diagnosis/fixes have their own regression evidence. See docs/evidence/panda-sdk3-runtime-01 and the design/plan.\n\nLocal Docker/source writes hit ENOSPC, so the original checkout is preserved and source work uses a memory-backed Git clone; actual targets run on disposable hosted runners. No SDK rebuild, main merge, environment or registry publication. Stage 7 remains incomplete.\n",
